
`native/` holds the AUnit tests for ImplementScraper/InterfaceScraper
(../lib/KilverbakbesturingCore/src/), run natively (no Teensy attached):

- `native/tests/` -- one `test_<ClassName>.cpp` per class under test.
- `native/support/` -- a small, self-contained set of Arduino-shaped stubs
  (Print/Stream/EEPROM/Arduino.h/etc.), not a real EpoxyDuino dependency, plus
  `native_main.cpp` (the host `int main()` entry point). `VehicleGps.hpp`
  here also implements `DistanceBetween()`/`GetPosition()`/`GetAltitudeCm()`
  with real math (a flat local-tangent-plane approximation, matching the real
  `triton::VehicleGps::DistanceBetween()` now does too) rather than a fixed
  stub value -- this module's leveling calculation needs genuine relative
  distances between deliberately-chosen lat/long test fixtures.
- `native/KilverbakbesturingNativeTests.cpp` -- the single AUnit driver
  (`setup()`/`loop()`), matching Ploegbesturing's/Pootmachinebesturing's/
  Slangenpomp Spuitcomputer's `*NativeTests.cpp` pattern. Every `test_*.cpp`
  file only registers `test(...)` blocks; none of them define `setup()`/
  `loop()` themselves, so they all link into one combined binary instead of
  one binary per test file.
- `native/run_tests_msvc.ps1` -- MSVC fallback for Windows without GCC.

```
pio run -e native
.pio/build/native/program(.exe)
```

Needs a real host C++17 compiler on PATH (g++ or clang++) -- on Windows
without one, use test\native\run_tests_msvc.ps1 instead, which builds and
runs the same combined binary via MSVC directly. That script passes
`/Zc:preprocessor` -- MSVC's legacy preprocessor mishandles AUnit's
`test(SuiteName, testName)` argument-count dispatch, which every test in
this project uses (matching this family's convention: groups each test's
display name under the class it exercises, e.g.
`ImplementScraper_calculateDistances_degenerateReferencePoints_fallsBackToZero`,
`InterfaceScraper_update_staleGgaFix_selectsHold`).

## Known gaps

- `CalibrationScraper` (the LCD/button calibration wizard extracted from the
  legacy `InterfaceScraper::calibrate()`) is `#ifdef ARDUINO`-guarded and
  deliberately excluded from `[env:native]`'s `build_src_filter` -- same
  reason as `CalibrationPlough`/`CalibrationPlanter`/`CalibrationSprayer`. No
  native coverage exists or is planned for it.
- `ImplementScraper::getActualPosition()`'s divide-by-zero guard (two
  calibration points holding the same reading) has no public setter to
  construct that state directly -- `positionCalibrationData` is only settable
  through `SetPositionCalibrationData()`, which reads a *live* `analogRead()`,
  and the whole sensored code path is `#ifndef NOSENS`-gated (dead on every
  board built today; this production unit has no position sensor at all,
  matching the legacy source's `NOSENS` default). Same gap Slangenpomp
  Spuitcomputer's PWM-calibration guard has, for the same reason.
- `InterfaceScraper::UpdateScreen()` (LCD rendering) compiles as part of
  `InterfaceScraper.cpp` (needed since `CheckButtons()`/`Update()`, which
  *are* tested, live in the same file) but its output isn't asserted on by
  any test -- `test/native/support/InterfaceI2CLCD.hpp`'s `WriteBuffer`/
  `WriteScreen` are no-ops.
- The `teensy41` real-board env (ACAN_T4-based CAN/ISOBUS setup in
  `src/main.cpp`, matching Ploegbesturing's) has not been build-verified on
  real hardware -- only via `pio run -e teensy41`'s cross-compile in this
  environment.
- Only the `teensy41` board is wired up today. This module's legacy source
  also referenced a production Arduino Micro board, an Arduino Micro/
  Leonardo "voorserie" preseries board, and a Teensy 3.5/3.6 protoboard --
  their `#ifdef` branches remain in `ConfigScraper.hpp`/
  `ConfigImplementScraper.hpp`/`ConfigInterfaceScraper.hpp` for future
  revival, but none of them has a buildable `platformio.ini` env yet.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing (not used here -- pio test's
own Unity-based runner doesn't understand this project's AUnit setup):
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html
